WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.735
-The GOP is intent

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.938
on using the power of the state

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.939
to punish critics
and suppress votes

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.409
as one of their former
rising stars, Matt Gaetz,

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.978
faces an intensifying
investigation

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.780
in which authorities
seized his phone last winter.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.983
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:21.321
♪♪

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.655
The Republican Party
is currently

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.857
in the political wilderness.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.191
They've lost the presidency

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.792 line:0%
and both houses of Congress

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.294 line:0%
and their previous
standard bearer

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.262 line:0%
never once cracked 50% approval.

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:31.698 line:0%
Meanwhile,
the Biden administration

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:34.601 line:0%
is winning high marks and polls
on its COVID response,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.036 line:0%
its early slate of executive
orders, and the economy,

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.638 line:0%
which is why Republicans

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.140 line:0%
are desperately grasping
for ways to attack him

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.677 line:0%
and ending up with some
very bizarre critiques.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.780
-John Cornyn tweeted
what, now, we know is a quote

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.316 line:0%
from a Politico piece
about Joe Biden...

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:07.133
And he goes on to say...

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.234
-You got him!

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.036
He's not tweeting
and saying commentaries

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.138
about Arnold Schwarzenegger's
"Apprentice" ratings

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.041
or retweeting suggestions
that Osama bin Laden

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.510
might still be alive --
a real thing Trump did.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.379
So the only conclusion
we can reach is

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.113
that there must be
a secret cabal

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:25.184
of antifa deep state socialists
who are really running things,

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:26.552
while Biden sits around

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.788
having normal thoughts
with his normal brain.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.356
Republicans are obsessed

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.158
with the idea
that Biden is a puppet,

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.793
when Trump was like a Muppet,

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.495
they introduced
on "Sesame Street"

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.363
to teach kids
about impulse control.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.731
[ As Cookie Monster ]
Where all my cookies go?

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.400
[ As Trump ]
Sorry, CM.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.435
I ate 'em all.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.836
These guys actually think
Americans want

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.671
a president constantly tweeting
psychotic,

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:49.141
all-caps stuff at 3:00 am
about having his wires tapped,

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:51.877
and screaming at reporters
on the White House lawn

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:54.080
with a helicopter whirring
in the background

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.615
like it's the final scene
in "MASH."

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.550
Second "M-A-S-H" reference
in two days!

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.119
Come on, TikTokers,
bring on your remixes.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.521
If you could do it
for sea shanties,

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:02.922
you can do it for Alan Alda.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.391
And, with all due respect
to Jeremy Renner,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.926
that'll always be my Hawkeye.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.028
Oh, he didn't have arrows,

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.163
but he always had
a quiver full o' quips.

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:13.299
Say what you will about the guy,
Biden keeps it simple.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.601
Yesterday, for example,
he was asked about his decision

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.304
to finally withdraw troops
from Afghanistan.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.840
Now, if reporters had asked
Trump that question,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.441
they would've gotten
a 10-minute answer

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:24.744
that somehow wound its way
to the time

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.745
he met Marlo Thomas at Elaine's.

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:27.747
[ As Trump ]
"That Girl."

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:28.981
What a show.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.617
She hated me and you know what?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:32.851
She was right.

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:35.554
[ Laughter ]
A lot of evidence out there

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:37.357
that I'm a bad guy.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:39.959
But when Biden was asked the
question, he was very direct.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.833
A solemn moment
and a direct answer.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.967
Reporters who cover
the White House

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.301
probably have to figure out
what to do

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:51.937
with all the leftover space
in their notepads.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:53.305
When they were covering
Trump's White House,

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:55.074
they probably
couldn't distinguish

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.810
between their notepads
and their dream journals.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.385
"Did I fall asleep reading
e.e. cummings again?"

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:08.521
So that's one reason
Biden's numbers are higher

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.390
than Trump's everywhere,
not to mention the fact

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.559
that Biden's policies
are more popular.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.226
And, as a result,
Republicans are stuck

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:16.362
complaining that Biden
doesn't tweet enough.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.231
And, as the Cornyn comments
show, Trump may be gone,

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:22.101
but Trumpism,
as an ideological project,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.036
as well as the performance
of Trumpism,

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:26.506
are very much ascendant
within the Republican Party.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.574
As we speak, the GOP
is actively trying to use

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:31.411
the power of the state to punish
anyone who disagrees with them,

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.813
the latest example being
Major League Baseball.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.348 line:0%
-Three Republican senators
are looking

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.383 line:0%
to put pressure
on Major League Baseball

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.053 line:0%
after it decided to pull the
All-Star Game out of Georgia,

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.754 line:0%
the league making the move
to protest

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.856 line:0%
Georgia's controversial
new voting law.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.191 line:0%
Senators Ted Cruz,
Mike Lee, and Josh Hawley

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:47.960 line:0%
are introducing
legislation today

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.995 line:0%
to eliminate
a nearly century-old

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:52.631 line:0%
antitrust exemption
for Major League Baseball,

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:54.734 line:0%
as a way of punishing
the league.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.503
-So the America First crowd is
going after America's pastime.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.904
What's next,
you guys going to try

00:03:58.904 --> 00:04:00.906
to cancel blue jeans
and pickup trucks?

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:01.974
Oh, right, I forgot.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:04.477
Cruz already canceled
blue jeans.

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.611
Yikes!

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:06.812
[ Laughter ]
He really puts the "dung"

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.814
in "dungarees."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.182
I have to say,
it's especially surprising

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:11.951
that Ted Cruz is going
after baseball,

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:12.985
given that he has the beard

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:15.220
of a 40-year-old
journeyman pitcher

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.223
on a 1986 Topps card.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.458
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:22.228
Wearing a uniform from 1918.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.297
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:27.900
So Republicans want to use
the power of the Senate

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.736
to punish anyone
who criticizes them.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:32.337
They're also plotting to steal
the presidency and Congress

00:04:32.337 --> 00:04:33.639
without actually
winning elections.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:34.840
That's what all these

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.742
voter suppression bills
are designed to do.

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.444
For example, you might remember

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.112
when Trump's lawyer
Rudy Giuliani

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:41.180
flew around the country,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.982
trying to convince
state legislatures

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.051
to overturn their election
results, or when

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:49.255
Trump advisor/underground lab
assistant Stephen Miller claimed

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.257
that states Biden won
were sending

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:54.127
so-called alternate slates
of electors

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.695
to Washington to vote for Trump.

00:04:56.695 --> 00:04:58.664
-We have more than enough time

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:02.434 line:0%
to right the wrong of this
fraudulent election result

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.104 line:0%
and certify Donald Trump
as the winner of the election.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:08.341 line:0%
As we speak today,
an alternate slate of electors

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.876 line:0%
in the contested states
is going to vote

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:13.879 line:0%
and we're going to send
those results up to Congress.

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:15.915
-Obviously, as we explained
at the time,

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.717
alternate slates of electors
aren't a real thing,

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.252
though, I bet Steven Miller
tried to use

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.254
an alternate slate of electors
in high school,

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:25.123
to get voted Most Charismatic,
instead of Most Likely

00:05:25.123 --> 00:05:27.826
to Chase Down an Iguana
on an Episode of "Planet Earth."

00:05:27.826 --> 00:05:29.762
But the important point is
Republicans are now trying

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.898
to make that fake thing real.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.298
They're actually trying
to pass laws

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:35.901
that would allow them to subvert
election results in their states

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:38.904
and award Electoral College
votes to a candidate who loses.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.539
They're not saying
that outright, of course,

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:42.941
but the actual text
of these laws

00:05:42.941 --> 00:05:44.743
definitely opens
the possibility.

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:46.645
-We just lived
through a president who tried

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:49.649
to overturn those results,
specifically, in Georgia

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.384 line:0%
and there are concerns
this new bill

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:55.188 line:0%
would allow, potentially,
for more chicanery.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:57.656 line:0%
As you well know, reading
from The New York Times,

00:05:57.656 --> 00:05:59.092 line:0%
just a brief summary, it says,

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.425 line:0%
"beyond the provisions
on the voting" --

00:06:00.425 --> 00:06:02.094 line:0%
that's up until Election Day --

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:05.497 line:0%
"the new law risks making
election subversion easier,"

00:06:05.497 --> 00:06:07.500 line:0%
including appearing
to go directly

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.902 line:0%
after some of those officials,

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:13.339 line:0%
like the secretary of state,
who drew Trump's ire precisely

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:16.042 line:0%
because they did their jobs
in a nonpartisan way.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.443 line:0%
-It gives state election
officials

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.845 line:0%
more power to intervene
in county elections.

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:22.014 line:0%
State leaders are now able
to appoint or remove

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.416 line:0%
local election officials.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:24.750
-It's obvious
what's happening here.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.819
They just want to make it
easier to do, next time,

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.121
what they tried to do last time.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.256
If you wake up
to find your roommate

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:31.691
holding a pillow above your head

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:34.326
because you heard his shoes
squeak on the floorboards,

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:37.129
don't relax when he goes out
and buys slippers.

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:39.498
This is all motivated
by the unhinged lie

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:41.801
that there was widespread fraud
in the 2020 election,

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.603
which there was not,
and one of the loudest champions

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.571
of that lie was Florida
Congressman Matt Gaetz,

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.439
who was supposed to be
one of the leaders

00:06:47.439 --> 00:06:49.441
in the next wave of Trumpism
in the GOP.

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:52.678
Gaetz objected to the lawful
counting of electoral votes,

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.646
even after the January 6th
insurrection,

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:57.016
and claimed that,
despite the Trump campaign

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.751
losing dozens of court cases,

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:01.487
they were actually proving
that there was fraud.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.623
-Election fraud really
requires two things.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:06.993 line:0%
One, a very large pool
of unaccounted-for ballots

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:08.628 line:0%
that aren't attached to a human;

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:11.764 line:0%
and then, second is the rapid
processing of those ballots.

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:14.467 line:0%
Then, they exclude the observers
and then, they just wrap

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:17.270 line:0%
those polluted ballots
into a broader universe,

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.239 line:0%
and I think that is where
we're proving the fraud.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:21.440
-None of that makes sense.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.443
I can't even follow the syntax
or the metaphors.

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:26.378
A large pool of ballots,

00:07:26.378 --> 00:07:28.681
and then they wrap
the pool of ballots

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.683
into a broader universe
of ballots?

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:32.117
What does any of that mean?

00:07:32.117 --> 00:07:34.286
You sound like a tour guide
at MoMA, trying to describe

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:36.756
a Dalí painting you're seeing
for the first time.

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:40.359
"So, uh, you know, the bricks
are wrapped inside the, um,

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:43.796
lake. Uh, the lake,
of course, represents

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:45.264
time?
I'm sorry I got confused.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.867
I thought this was the museum
with all the big bony things,

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:49.501
whatever they called.
You know."

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:50.503
Now, as we've been telling you,

00:07:50.503 --> 00:07:51.504 line:0%
Gaetz is under investigation

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:52.838 line:0%
for alleged sex trafficking

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:54.339 line:0%
involving his wingman,

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:57.543 line:0%
the former Seminole County
tax collector Joel Greenberg,

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.311 line:0%
who's been charged
with 33 counts

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:01.146 line:0%
and is reportedly cooperating
with authorities,

00:08:01.146 --> 00:08:03.382 line:0%
including offering
information on Gaetz

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:06.452 line:0%
and, every day, we get new
details about the investigation.

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:08.053 line:0%
-A source familiar with the case

00:08:08.053 --> 00:08:10.922 line:0%
confirms Greenberg
told investigators details

00:08:10.922 --> 00:08:13.893 line:0%
about how he and Gaetz
would pay women for sex

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:17.062 line:0%
with cash and gifts,
in possible violation

00:08:17.062 --> 00:08:19.965 line:0%
of prostitution
and sex trafficking laws.

00:08:19.965 --> 00:08:22.668 line:0%
According to receipts
reviewed by CNN,

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.437 line:0%
Gaetz and Greenberg
used digital payment apps,

00:08:25.437 --> 00:08:28.073 line:0%
including Venmo,
to send hundreds of dollars

00:08:28.073 --> 00:08:30.709 line:0%
to at least one woman
who attended these parties.

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:31.977 line:0%
-Politico has revealed

00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:33.879 line:0%
the explosive news
that federal agents

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:35.314 line:0%
executed a search warrant

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:38.317 line:0%
and seized Gaetz's phone
this past winter.

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.987
-I'm no lawyer, but it can't be
good when they seize your phone.

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:43.055
No one's happy to have
their phone seized.

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:45.024
I don't even like it
when I show someone a picture

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:46.692
and they grab the phone
out of my hand

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:47.860
and then I have to mutter,

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.728
[ Shakily ]
"Don't scroll, don't scroll,"

00:08:49.728 --> 00:08:51.062
[ Laughter ]
until I get it back.

00:08:51.062 --> 00:08:54.666
I'm not even happy when my wife
asks me to use mine.

00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:56.068
"You want to tell me
what this is?"

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:58.571
Uh, YouTube clips
of old "M-A-S-H" episodes.

00:08:58.571 --> 00:09:00.139
[ Laughter ]
"I thought you said
you were working!"

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:01.641
I am working!

00:09:01.641 --> 00:09:04.043
The "M-A-S-H" references
are the most popular part

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:05.644
of "A Closer Look"!
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:07.980
You are being a real
Charles Winchester.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.783
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:14.053
Chances are pretty high that,
if you've broken the law,

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:15.454
there's evidence
of it on your phone,

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:18.758 line:0%
especially since Gaetz
was reportedly using a cash app

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:21.661 line:0%
and Venmo to make payments
to his indicted buddy.

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.362 line:0%
Used to be, when politicians
broke the law,

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:25.431 line:0%
they stuffed an envelope full
of $100 bills

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:27.266
and met their contact
in a parking garage.

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:29.735
Now, they just Venmo
a buddy with an emoji

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.203
of an envelope stuffed
with cash.

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:33.205
We also keep finding out more

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:34.707
about what these dudes
were up to

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:36.775
and what kind of parties
they were hanging out at.

00:09:36.775 --> 00:09:38.310
-Now, we have learned
these parties were held

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:41.947 line:0%
at a house in a gated community
in suburban Orlando.

00:09:41.947 --> 00:09:44.917 line:0%
The women we spoke with said,
when some of the women arrived,

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:46.352 line:0%
there were rules.

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:48.287 line:0%
For example, the first thing
some of them were asked to do

00:09:48.287 --> 00:09:50.322 line:0%
is put away their cellphones.

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:52.624 line:0%
Now, one of the women told us
the attendees included

00:09:52.624 --> 00:09:55.795 line:0%
a who's who of local
Republican officials

00:09:55.795 --> 00:09:57.929 line:0%
and often included
Congressman Gaetz,

00:09:57.929 --> 00:09:59.364 line:0%
and these men just did not want

00:09:59.364 --> 00:10:02.601 line:0%
their activities at these
parties being documented.

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:05.938 line:0%
And we're told folks mingled
and shared drugs,

00:10:05.938 --> 00:10:08.240 line:0%
including cocaine and ecstasy.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.841
-If they ever make
a Florida version

00:10:09.841 --> 00:10:11.043
of the board game "Clue,"

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:13.078
"gated community
in suburban Orlando"

00:10:13.078 --> 00:10:14.246
should be one of the locations,

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.949
right next to "animal
sanctuary in Tampa."

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:18.050
You know, my grandmother
used to say,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.584
"Nothing good ever happens
after midnight,"

00:10:19.584 --> 00:10:22.020
and I'd say the same is true
about anything that happens

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:25.357
at a party in a gated community
in suburban Orlando

00:10:25.357 --> 00:10:27.293
where they make you
give up your phone.

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:28.961
"Well, they probably don't
want us to use our phones

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:30.662
to Google answers
for what I'm sure will be

00:10:30.662 --> 00:10:31.730
a night of trivia games.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:32.864
Oh, cocaine!

00:10:32.864 --> 00:10:34.165
Looks like it'll be
a late night."

00:10:34.165 --> 00:10:36.135
[ Laughter ]
As a general rule,

00:10:36.135 --> 00:10:39.571
never go to a party in a gated
community in suburban Orlando

00:10:39.571 --> 00:10:40.940
where they make you
give up your phone.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.341
Orlando's for two things --

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:43.542
going to theme parks

00:10:43.542 --> 00:10:45.978
or buying exotic fish
from an unlicensed dealer

00:10:45.978 --> 00:10:47.913
who works out of the back
of a pet food store.

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:50.349
"I got piranhas,
lionfish, snakeheads,

00:10:50.349 --> 00:10:52.551
and, for another $100,
I'll throw in this bad boy."

00:10:52.551 --> 00:10:54.152
[ Laughter ]
We're also learning more

00:10:54.152 --> 00:10:56.255
about a trip Gaetz
allegedly took,

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:58.290
which are also under scrutiny
by the feds,

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.825
and who he traveled with.

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:01.726
-CBS News has learned
that investigators

00:11:01.726 --> 00:11:04.129 line:0%
are scrutinizing a trip
Congressman Matt Gaetz took

00:11:04.129 --> 00:11:05.564 line:0%
to the Bahamas with this man,

00:11:05.564 --> 00:11:08.400 line:0%
Jason Pirozzolo,
a marijuana entrepreneur,

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.237 line:0%
Orlando hand surgeon,
and donor to Gaetz.

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:13.972 line:0%
-CBS News reporting that Gaetz's
trip to the Bahamas

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:15.207 line:0%
is part of a federal probe

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:17.676 line:0%
into the sex trafficking
allegation.

00:11:17.676 --> 00:11:18.778 line:0%
Here's a little bit of it...

00:11:37.429 --> 00:11:40.632
-An Orlando hand surgeon/
marijuana entrepreneur.

00:11:40.632 --> 00:11:42.701
Man, Florida never disappoints.

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:44.736
I'm shocked Gaetz
wasn't also buds

00:11:44.736 --> 00:11:45.905
with an alligator named Rick,

00:11:45.905 --> 00:11:48.774
who sold CBD oil
on the Miami Beach boardwalk.

00:11:48.774 --> 00:11:51.009
And, now, the heat on Gaetz
is intensifying,

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:53.245
to the point where Republicans
don't know how to respond.

00:11:53.245 --> 00:11:56.047
Yesterday, House Minority Whip
Steve Scalise

00:11:56.047 --> 00:11:57.215
was asked about Gaetz

00:11:57.215 --> 00:11:58.951
and stammered his way
through an answer.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.688
-Well, you know,
we've heard a lot of stories.

00:12:03.688 --> 00:12:05.991
I mean, obviously,
I've read the media reports,

00:12:05.991 --> 00:12:08.260
but, there's been nothing
that we've seen, yet,

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.761
from the Department of Justice.

00:12:09.761 --> 00:12:10.829
If something's going on,

00:12:10.829 --> 00:12:12.965
obviously,
we'll find out about it.

00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:16.802
You know, right now, it seems
hard to speculate on rumors,

00:12:16.802 --> 00:12:18.471
but, you know, if something

00:12:18.471 --> 00:12:20.172
really formal happened
from Justice,

00:12:20.172 --> 00:12:22.841
we would, of course, react
and take action.

00:12:22.841 --> 00:12:24.776
-It's so funny to watch
Republicans get flustered

00:12:24.776 --> 00:12:26.044
by questions about Gaetz,

00:12:26.044 --> 00:12:28.213
after they let him take
center stage for so long.

00:12:28.213 --> 00:12:29.648
[ As Scalise ]
Look, we -- I don't know
the facts,

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:31.016
but if the, you know,
the allegations

00:12:31.016 --> 00:12:33.519
about, uh,
ecstasy-fueled house parties

00:12:33.519 --> 00:12:35.020
with the dude
who was later indicted

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.955
for sex trafficking
and flights to the Bahamas

00:12:36.955 --> 00:12:38.990
with the marijuana-loving
hand surgeon are true,

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:40.292
then, yeah, you know, I --

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:41.793
I think we might, you know,
we might do something.

00:12:41.793 --> 00:12:43.495
We'll do something
about it, right?

00:12:43.495 --> 00:12:45.030
And, as for Gaetz,
he continues to maintain

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.965
the whole thing is a setup
egged on by the media

00:12:46.965 --> 00:12:49.168
and, in particular,
he got into a heated exchange

00:12:49.168 --> 00:12:52.071
with a CNN reporter as he left
the Capitol on Tuesday.

00:12:52.071 --> 00:12:53.572
-Well, I think you
can read my essay

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:54.640
in The Washington Examiner.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.274
I think you can check out
the work

00:12:56.274 --> 00:12:59.912
that your network has done
to propagandize lies about me.

00:12:59.912 --> 00:13:01.480
I think that really ought
to concern you, Manu.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.215
You've always considered
yourself a real journalist,

00:13:03.215 --> 00:13:04.550
but that doesn't strike me
as real journalism.
-What about the

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:05.551
updates from today?
-Are you concerned about the

00:13:05.551 --> 00:13:07.219
House Ethics investigation?

00:13:07.219 --> 00:13:10.488
Are you going to cooperate
with the investigation, sir?

00:13:10.488 --> 00:13:12.591
-I'd say, along with getting
your phone seized,

00:13:12.591 --> 00:13:13.859
being chased
down a flight of stairs

00:13:13.859 --> 00:13:15.427
by a crowd of reporters
and getting hustled

00:13:15.427 --> 00:13:16.862
in the back seat
of a waiting car

00:13:16.862 --> 00:13:18.364
isn't a sign
that things are going great.

00:13:18.364 --> 00:13:20.599
That's classic
corrupt-politician stuff.

00:13:20.599 --> 00:13:23.736
No one ever, in that situation,
is in it for a good reason.

00:13:23.736 --> 00:13:25.970
"Sir, sir, can you tell us
how you cured cancer?"

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.072
I didn't cure cancer!

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:28.206
Stop spreading lies about me!

00:13:28.206 --> 00:13:29.408
Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:13:29.408 --> 00:13:31.410
I have to be rushed
into this unmarked van.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.077 line:0%
This is the state
of the modern GOP,

00:13:33.077 --> 00:13:34.446 line:0%
an authoritarian movement

00:13:34.446 --> 00:13:37.182 line:0%
intent on dismantling democracy
and suppressing dissent.

00:13:37.182 --> 00:13:39.318
Gaetz was supposed to be one
of the leaders

00:13:39.318 --> 00:13:40.619
of the next wave of Trumpism

00:13:40.619 --> 00:13:43.455
and, now, like so many others
in Trump's inner circle,

00:13:43.455 --> 00:13:45.090
he's found himself
in legal hot water.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.291
Who knows what'll happen to him?

00:13:46.291 --> 00:13:48.227
But, if he does get
taken away by the feds,

00:13:48.227 --> 00:13:49.795
I hope we can send
him off like this --

00:13:49.795 --> 00:13:52.298
[ Rotors whirring ]

00:13:57.102 --> 00:14:00.138
[ Johnny Mandel's
"Suicide Is Painless" plays ]

